#question(title: [Composition law], shrink: true)[
  #set text(size: 13pt)
  Write a proof for the following Theorem
  #slide-block(title: [Theorem])[
    Let $display({a_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ be a
    sequence. Let $display(L in RR)$. Let $f$
    be a function.
    - IF
      $display(cases({a_n}_(n = 0)^oo --> L, f " is continuous at " L))$
    - THEN
      $display({f(a_n)}_(n = 0)^oo --> f(L))$
      .
  ]

  + Write the definition of your hypotheses
    and your conclusion.
  + Using the definition of your conclusion,
    figure out the structure of the proof.
  + Do some rough work if necessary.
  + Write a formal proof.
]
